BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Busy Bees\, Brown County State Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260806T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260806T153000
UID:e891850d95508163d8d24c431979831a@events.in.gov
DESCRIPTION:Join a park naturalist and the Brown County State Park honeybe
 e hive to learn about honeybees and how they live their complex lives! You
 &#39\;ll also get to ask questions about why protecting bees and other pol
 linating insects is such a good idea! Hear about threats bees face and lea
 rn how to help them in your area! Stay for a bee craft!
LOCATION:Brown County State Park\, Nature Center program room\, 1405 S.R. 
 46 W\, Nashville\, IN 
URL:on.in.gov/BrownCountySP
X-SOURCE:Brown County State Park
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Snake Meet and Greet\, Brown County State Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260807T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260807T113000
UID:5787330bd3e60e59f018163faae43f5b@events.in.gov
DESCRIPTION:Come to the Nature Center for an up close and personal look at
  one of Indiana&#39\;s native snakes! Learn about their unique traits\, th
 e threats they face\, and how snakes affect your life! Participants may pe
 t the snake at the end of the program. Please be aware this program involv
 es a live animal.
LOCATION:Brown County State Park\, Nature Center\, 1405 S.R. 46 W\, Nashvi
 lle\, IN 
URL:https://on.in.gov/browncountysp
X-SOURCE:Brown County State Park
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Timber! Understanding the Timber Rattlesnake\, Brown County State 
 Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260807T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260807T150000
UID:502a21a29e3a26587e71708a9cbf14bd@events.in.gov
DESCRIPTION:Come to the Nature Center for an up close and personal look In
 diana&#39\;s most venomous and most misunderstood snake! Learn about the h
 istory of timber rattlesnakes\, including how this animal became an Americ
 an symbol in the late 1700s. Learn how over a million visitors a year safe
 ly share the state park with these animals. We&#39\;ll also discuss venom\
 , how it works and is delievered\, and how Indiana&#39\;s venomous snakes 
 compare to the rest of the world! At the end\, we will feed the timber rat
 tlesnake a live mouse. Please be aware this program involves live animals.
  A live snake feeding may not be suitable for all guests\, particuarly chi
 ldren. Guests will have an opportunity to leave the program before the fee
 ding\, if they choose to do so. The program room has seating for about 45 
 people maximum. On busy days\, it is wise to arrive early!
LOCATION:Brown County State Park\, Nature Center\, 1405 S.R. 46 W\, Nashvi
 lle\, IN 
URL:https://on.in.gov/browncountysp
X-SOURCE:Brown County State Park
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Woodpeckers of Indiana\, Brown County State Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260808T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260808T114500
UID:9df8313a8e76fec95e7abb812e55683d@events.in.gov
DESCRIPTION:Join park expert\, bird enthusiast\, and NPR&#39\;s &quot\;Mom
 ent of Science&quot\; radio personality Don Glass in a presentation and di
 scussion about Indiana&#39\;s seven species of native woodpeckers! Learn w
 hat they look like\, their behaviors\, and some of the issues they face to
 day.
LOCATION:Brown County State Park\, Nature Center\, 1405 S.R. 46 W\, Nashvi
 lle\, IN 
URL:https://on.in.gov/browncountysp
X-SOURCE:Brown County State Park
END:VEVENT
