BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Full Moon Hike\, Brown County State Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260926T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260926T203000
UID:d0b38f4b6d080ff34d5cdb28a2920016@events.in.gov
DESCRIPTION:Join a park naturalist for a guided night hike on the Salt Cre
 ek Trail! The Full Moon is the brightest night of the month\, leading to i
 nteresting views along the creek. Learn about September&#39\;s full moon t
 his year\, the Harvest Moon. The Salt Creek Trail is rated very easy\, but
  should be considered moderate in the dark. The trail has some minor slope
 s\, a short stretch of lawn\, and possible wet or icy spots depending on w
 eather. Our route is&nbsp\; about 2 miles total and will take about an hou
 r to complete. Please do not bring pets on night hikes. Red flashlights ar
 e preferred for night vision and can be loaned to hikers on request. Hike 
 cancellation policy : Hikes will be cancelled if there is lightning\, temp
 eratures below 0 degrees Farenheit\, temperature indexes above 105 degrees
  Farenheit\, or a wind advisory. If a hike is cancelled\, gatehouses will 
 be informed. The phone number for the North Gatehouse is 812-988-5230.
LOCATION:Brown County State Park\, Olympic Pool parking lot\, 1405 S.R. 46
  W\, Nashville\, IN 
URL:https://on.in.gov/BrownCountySP
X-SOURCE:Brown County State Park
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:New Moon Hike\, Brown County State Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261010T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261010T213000
UID:31abe7039d462b6ed61197c11913d852@events.in.gov
DESCRIPTION:Full Moons occur when the Moon is fully illuminated by the Sun
 \, allowing viewers on Earth to see the full circle. It&#39\;s typically t
 he brightest night of the month. The New Moon is the darkest night of the 
 month\, when dark side of the Moon faces Earth. We&#39\;re going on a hike
  on the darkest night of the month! We will meet at the Park Office/Fire T
 ower Parking lot at 7:30pm to hike Trail 10. Please note Trail 10 should b
 e considered very rugged in the dark and involves hiking from one of the h
 ighest elevations in the park to one of the lowest. The route is 2.2 miles
  and will take about two hours. Red flashlights help us preserve night vis
 ion. We have some to lend out\, but it is wise to bring your own if you ha
 ve one. Hike cancellation policy: Hikes will be cancelled if there is ligh
 tning\, temperatures below 0 degrees Farenheit\, temperature indexes above
  105 degrees Farenheit\, or a wind advisory. If a hike is cancelled\, gate
 houses will be informed. The phone number for the North Gatehouse is 812-9
 88-5230.
LOCATION:Brown County State Park\, Park office\, 1405 S.R. 46 W\, Nashvill
 e\, IN 
URL:on.in.gov/BrownCountySP
X-SOURCE:Brown County State Park
END:VEVENT
